{"version":"1.5","group":"V201","entries":[{"id":"learn:00905999-v","headword":"exculpate","group":"V201","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW004103","JBKROW006881"],"localGlosses":["무죄로 만들다"],"definitionEn":"pronounce not guilty of criminal charges","definitionKo":"형사 혐의에 대해 무죄라고 밝히다","memoryKo":"증거가 혐의의 무게를 걷어 내어 죄가 없음을 밝혀 주는 장면을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"증거나 논증이 누군가를 죄책이나 비난에서 벗어나게 하는 법률·논증 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"유죄를 인정한 뒤 용서하는 pardon이 아니라 애초에 죄가 없음을 밝혀 책임에서 벗어나게 하는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"acquit","noteKo":"acquit는 법원이 무죄 판결을 내리는 데 자주 쓰이고, exculpate는 증거 등이 죄책이나 책임을 벗겨 주는 데도 쓰입니다."}],"example":{"en":"New evidence may exculpate the accused.","ko":"새로운 증거가 피고인의 무죄를 밝혀 줄 수도 있다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/e/ex/exculpate.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/e/ex/exculpate.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"4193e57a6544fc251d6ebca33724a424bfbeb3a1f7b926ec4d1e6f445b68b154"}]}},{"id":"learn:02434522-s","headword":"slovenly","group":"V201","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004104","JBKROW007847"],"localGlosses":["지저분한"],"definitionEn":"negligent of neatness especially in dress and person; habitually dirty and unkempt","definitionKo":"특히 옷차림과 몸가짐의 단정함에 무관심하여 습관적으로 지저분한","memoryKo":"옷차림과 몸가짐이 늘 흐트러진 모습을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"사람의 외모, 옷차림, 습관이나 일 처리 방식이 단정하지 않고 부주의함을 나타낼 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"한 번 더러워진 상태보다 습관적인 단정하지 못함과 부주의에 초점이 있습니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"sloppy","noteKo":"sloppy는 일·표현·방식까지 폭넓게 허술함을 뜻하고, slovenly는 특히 사람의 외양과 습관적 불결함에 잘 쓰입니다."}],"example":{"en":"His slovenly appearance hurt the interview.","ko":"그의 단정하지 못한 모습은 면접에 악영향을 주었다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/sl/slovenly.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/sl/slovenly.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"b505558c27ffa46c4ffcae92bdbd934c2a5f54488b3fe572801e6d338ab634a7"}]}},{"id":"learn:00531862-s","headword":"serene","group":"V201","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004114","JBKROW007823"],"localGlosses":["침착한"],"definitionEn":"not agitated; without losing self-possession","definitionKo":"동요하지 않고 침착한","memoryKo":"소란 속에서도 잔잔한 수면처럼 평온한 상태를 기억하세요.","usageKo":"사람의 표정·태도나 장소의 분위기가 평온하고 흔들림 없음을 나타낼 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"기쁘다는 뜻이 아니라 걱정이나 동요 없이 차분하다는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"composed","noteKo":"composed는 압박 속 자기 통제를, serene은 더 넓게 평온하고 고요한 상태를 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"She remained serene during the crisis.","ko":"그녀는 위기 속에서도 침착함을 유지했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/se/serene.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/se/serene.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"d8eca0129854810907e303c92081f495ecbff444613744992e7074ea6a217992"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fc/En-us-serene.ogg/En-us-serene.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-serene.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}},{"id":"learn:00451803-s","headword":"juxtaposed","group":"V201","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004122","JBKROW007301"],"localGlosses":["인접한"],"definitionEn":"placed side by side often for comparison","definitionKo":"흔히 비교하기 위해 나란히 놓인","memoryKo":"두 대상을 바로 옆에 놓아 차이가 눈에 띄게 하는 구도를 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"글, 사진, 생각 등을 나란히 배치해 공통점이나 대비를 드러내는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단순히 가까이 있다는 adjacent와 달리 비교나 대조를 위한 배치라는 의미가 중요합니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"adjacent","noteKo":"adjacent는 단지 서로 붙어 있음을 뜻하지만 juxtaposed는 비교·대조 효과를 내는 나란한 배치를 암시합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The article juxtaposed wealth and poverty.","ko":"그 기사는 부와 빈곤을 나란히 놓아 대비했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/j/ju/juxtaposed.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/j/ju/juxtaposed.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"0f2344c6589392ddce42120d0a5ddc87f00db5134f605134d41ce67463b09808"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7f/En-us-juxtaposed.ogg/En-us-juxtaposed.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-juxtaposed.ogg","license":"Public domain","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}},{"id":"learn:01693210-s","headword":"banal","group":"V201","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW001435","JBKROW002168","JBKROW004146","JBKROW006359"],"localGlosses":["진부한"],"definitionEn":"repeated too often; overfamiliar through overuse","definitionKo":"너무 자주 반복되어 지나치게 익숙한","memoryKo":"너무 많이 들어 새로움이 닳아 버린 표현을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"생각, 표현, 이야기 등이 진부하고 독창성 없이 뻔함을 평가할 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"틀리거나 중요하지 않다는 뜻이 아니라 지나친 반복 때문에 신선함이 없다는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"trite","noteKo":"둘 다 진부하지만 trite는 특히 상투적인 말·생각에, banal은 평범하고 지루할 만큼 새로움 없는 대상에 널리 씁니다."}],"example":{"en":"The speech was full of banal slogans.","ko":"그 연설은 진부한 구호로 가득했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/b/ba/banal.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/b/ba/banal.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"65412448ad5826a3c773105f9fe3fd9ecd05822c69717a7a74ff0dc363577c33"}]}}]}
